## Runtime: part of the AIL native runtime; linked into user executables
## under the Runtime Exception (see LICENSE).
##
## Vector loops for user code (native.vec.1, ADR 0942). The AIL bodies are
## the scalar definitions and the reference; `compiler/x64/kernels.ail` and
## `compiler/a64/kernels.ail` assemble them with AVX2 and NEON. `keep` is the list whose
## elements `c` points into: passing it tells the optimizer the call changes
## that list. The kernels ignore it.

## `c[i] = c[i] + x * b[i]` for `i < n`, on `int` words. Called only where a
## data-range guard (native.bce.12) has proved `|x|` and every `|b[i]|` at most
## 2^20 and no sum overflowing, so the kernels may multiply 32-bit halves.
fn vec_axpyi(c int, b int, n int, x int, keep List[int])
    for i in 0..n
        store64(c + 8 * i, load64(c + 8 * i) + x * load64(b + 8 * i))

## `c[i] = c[i] + x * b[i]` for `i < n`, on `float`s: the product `x * b[i]`
## and the sum `c[i] + q` rounded in that operand order, as the scalar loop
## `s += x * y` does them, so a NaN keeps its payload.
fn vec_axpyf(c int, b int, n int, x float, keep List[int])
    for i in 0..n
        q := x * loadf(b + 8 * i)
        storef(c + 8 * i, loadf(c + 8 * i) + q)
